A||N||9||chris6878||3800 v6 in pontiac grand prix?||||5||
Z||000000||chris6878||03-12-2000||07:29 PM||||I seen a newer grand prix today that had the decal "3800"..   i have heard this will bolt to the fiero tranny with no mods...  is this engine the same type of fuel injection as the fiero..? and what kind of horsepower does this motor have from the factory?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phil||03-12-2000||08:19 PM||||The tranny is the only thing that bolts up without lots of modifications. It will cost a couple of thousand $ not counting the engine. Performance is fantastic. For more info check <A HREF="http://www.americancustomeng.com" TARGET=_blank>www.americancustomeng.com</A>   ||||reg||1
Z||000002||kupop87gt||03-12-2000||08:20 PM||||I'm going on a hunch that the Grand Prix has the Series II 3800, which has 205 horsepower. Unless it's a GTP supercharged, in which it has 240. The same type of fuel injection??? I'm not sure if it's MPFI or SFI. It has a distributorless ignition. There's 3800 conversion sites on the net.<BR>Try <A HREF="http://www.americancustomeng.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.americancustomeng.com/</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||terryk||03-12-2000||10:05 PM||||GP's have the Series II 3800 in NA and SC forms. If it says 3800 on the side, it's not a supercharged (it's a normally aspirated engine). ||||reg||1
Z||000004||chris6878||03-12-2000||11:48 PM||||Thanks for the replies.. i was just curious   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||batboy||03-13-2000||06:52 AM||||The longer time goes by and I can't find a decent 87 2.5 engine for my SE, the more I think about an engine swap. The 3800 swap is looking more and more appealing. Good used motors are plentiful, they're reliable, and make decent power. Motor mounts are always a big issue in a swap and of course you have use the ECM that matches the engine. I ran across this guy's method of swapping a 3800 and the AOD tranny in as a unit. I like it!<P><B>Tom Corey's 3800/AOD-auto swap</B><P>First of all I assume you don't have an 88 Fiero. If you do, the solution is different. I recommend you use the motor mounts and<BR>axles from a Pontiac Transport Van (or Olds Silhouette Van) They have the exact same track (width - axle end to axle end as<BR>the Fiero. Use the inside joints from the engine/transaxle you purchased and the outside joints from an 88 Fiero 5 speed. This<BR>will match up the splines. If you use these mounts and axles your installation will put the engine nearly centered in the engine<BR>compartment and you will not have to trim the deck lid. <P>The cradle on the 88 is smaller and I don't think the mounts I told you about will work properly. On my 88 GT I used the 95 Bonneville side mount, a stock fiero front mount and a MOPAR small truck mount at the rear of the transaxle with a dogbone under the right side. (The torque from the 3800 kept bending the rear GM transaxle mount I started with. And the axles on the 88 are from different sources than I told you earlier.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Dan86gt3.8||03-14-2000||11:14 PM||||Glad you should ask.  Yes the 3800 bolts to the 5 speed getrag and the isuzu 4 speed, ohhh ya and I happen to have one in my 86 fiero gt, but I have the automatic overdrive 4 speed auto tranny that comes with the 3800 engines.  Its called the 4T60E. The power ratings are all different depending on year of engine.  ACE has info about the VIN # decoding, the one you want is the one with the indication "K" in the 8th place (I think its 8th but don't quote me) of the vin# (number right below inspection sticker on a metal tab, also its in like 2 or 3 other locations)  Anyways if you have a vin k non supercharged 3800, like you asked about it has 205hp/215torque.  Its a great engine to have in the fiero, I love mine, from who I have beaten and who has beat me it should be a mid to high 14 second car.  I would love to have the supercharged version, but O well.  There are 3 ways of doing it ACE, a guy named Chris West, and self engineered, I have seen it done all 3 ways and all of them seem to work really well.  If you have any other questions e-mail me!  ||||reg||12
Z||000007||terryk||03-15-2000||03:32 PM||||Dan, <P>How did you handle the axles since the 4T60E is longer than a 125C or 440/4T60?<P>Next, what flywheel does everyone use with the Getrag? I don't know if the 3.0L N car flywheel will work. Some N cars came with Getrags and 3.0L Buick V6's.<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 03-15-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||Phil||03-15-2000||04:52 PM||||If you want a standard shift in the 3800 you have to "make" a flywheel nothing fits directly.||||reg||1
Z||000009||WKDFIRO||03-16-2000||07:06 PM||||I know someone who has a 3800 (1st gen) in their 85 GT. I have a 99 Grand Prix with the Series II. Your are correct. The GTPs have the Superchargers. The natural 3.8s aren't slouches either though....For a big car like that it goes very nicely!||||reg||6
